module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistAwayBridge.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.GradedAlgebra.Proj.LaurentAway

/-!
# The twist of a degree-one standard chart is free of rank one

Let `A = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝒜 n` be a graded ring and let `f ∈ 𝒜 1` be homogeneous of degree one. The
chart-sections model of `Γ(D₊(f), 𝒪(t))` is the degree-zero localization
`GradedModuleDegreeZeroLocalization 𝒜 (twistGrading 𝒜 t) f`, a module over the degree-zero
localization `A₍f₎ = HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 f`. This file proves that it is **free of
rank one**, on the single generator `f ^ t`.

`f ^ t` makes sense for a negative `t` because `f` is a unit in `A[1/f]`, and the generator is
written as the honest fraction `f ^ a / f ^ b` with `a - b = t`, which is what lets one statement
serve both signs.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartDegreeOne.numExp` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartDegreeOne.denExp`: the two natural exponents writing the
  integer power `f ^ t` as a fraction `f ^ a / f ^ b`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartDegreeOne.twistGen`: **the generator**, the homogeneous
  fraction `f ^ a / f ^ b` read in the chart-sections model.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartDegreeOne.twistAwayBasis` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartDegreeOne.twistDegreeZeroBasis`: **the rank-one basis**, in
  the base-change model and in the chart-sections model respectively.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartDegreeOne.span_range_const_eq_twistAway`: the integer power
  `f ^ t` spans the `t`-th degree part of `A[1/f]`, which is
  `Stacks.GradedLaurent.twistAway_eq_span_zpow` with the degree specialised to one.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartDegreeOne.twistDegreeZeroBasis_apply`: the basis vector of
  the chart-sections model is the generator.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartDegreeOne.free_twistDegreeZero`: **the chart sections of the
  `t`-th twist are free over the chart ring**, for `f` of degree one.

## Why degree one, and what fails above it

Freeness of rank one is **false** for a homogeneous `f` of general positive degree, so the
hypothesis `f ∈ 𝒜 1` is not an artefact of the proof. Over `ℚ` take `A = ℚ[T₀, T₁]` with its usual
grading and `f = T₀ ^ 2 + T₁ ^ 2`, homogeneous of degree two. Then `D₊(f)` is the complement in
`Proj A = ℙ¹_ℚ` of a single closed point of residue degree two, so its Picard group is
`ℤ / 2ℤ`, generated by the class of `𝒪(1)`; the module `𝒜(1)₍f₎` is therefore invertible and
nontrivial, hence not free. What survives for every positive degree is only the weaker statement
that the module is invertible, which is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization.isInvertible_twistingSheafOverBasicOpen`.

## Implementation notes

The two models of the degree-zero localization of a twist — the chart-sections model
`GradedModuleDegreeZeroLocalization 𝒜 (twistGrading 𝒜 t) f`, a submodule of a
`LocalizedModule`, and the base-change model `Stacks.ProjStandardOpenBaseChange.twistAway`, a
submodule of a `Localization` — are identified by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistAwayBridge.twistAwayEquiv`. The span and independence statements of
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/GradedAlgebra/Proj/LaurentAway.lean` live in the second model, so the
basis is built there and transported; nothing below reproves either input.

`Stacks.GradedLaurent.twistAway_eq_span_zpow` is indexed by `k * ↑d`, so at `d = 1` its degree
reads `t * ((1 : ℕ) : ℤ)` rather than `t`; the cast is cleared once, in
`span_range_const_eq_twistAway`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01M6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01M6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ML](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ML)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open HomogeneousLocalization AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj
open Stacks.GradedLaurent Stacks.ProjStandardOpenBaseChange
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistAwayBridge

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartDegreeOne

universe u v

variable {R : Type u} {A : Type v} [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A) [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] {f : A}

/-! ### The generator as a fraction -/

/-- The denominator exponent writing the integer power `f ^ t` as a fraction of natural powers:
it is `-t` for a negative `t` and `0` otherwise. -/
public def denExp (t : ℤ) : ℕ := (-t).toNat

/-- The numerator exponent writing the integer power `f ^ t` as a fraction of natural powers:
it is `t` for a nonnegative `t` and `0` otherwise. -/
public def numExp (t : ℤ) : ℕ := (t + (-t).toNat).toNat

/-- The two exponents differ by `t`, which is the only property of them that is used. -/
public theorem numExp_eq (t : ℤ) : (numExp t : ℤ) = t + denExp t := by
  simp only [numExp, denExp]
  omega

/-- **The integer power `f ^ t` of the inverted element, as a single fraction.** -/
public theorem coe_awayUnit_zpow_eq_mk_exp (f : A) (t : ℤ) :
    ((awayUnit f ^ t : (Localization.Away f)ˣ) : Localization.Away f) =
      Localization.mk (f ^ numExp t)
        ⟨f ^ denExp t, Submonoid.pow_mem _ (Submonoid.mem_powers f) (denExp t)⟩ :=
  coe_awayUnit_zpow_eq_mk f (numExp_eq t)

/-- The numerator `f ^ a` is homogeneous of the degree the `t`-th twist asks of a fraction with
denominator `f ^ b`. This is where `f` being of degree one is used. -/
public theorem pow_numExp_mem_twistGrading (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (t : ℤ) :
    f ^ numExp t ∈ twistGrading (S := A) 𝒜 t (denExp t • (1 : ℤ)) := by
  have h : (denExp t • (1 : ℤ)) + t = (numExp t : ℤ) := by
    rw [nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one, numExp_eq]; ring
  rw [twistGrading_apply, h, integerGrading_natCast, mem_homogeneousSubmodule]
  simpa using SetLike.pow_mem_graded (numExp t) hf

/-- **The generator of the chart sections of the `t`-th twist**, the homogeneous fraction
`f ^ a / f ^ b` with `a - b = t`. -/
public def twistGen (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (t : ℤ) :
    GradedModuleDegreeZeroLocalization 𝒜 (twistGrading (S := A) 𝒜 t) f :=
  degreeZeroFraction 𝒜 (twistGrading (S := A) 𝒜 t) hf (denExp t) (f ^ numExp t)
    (pow_numExp_mem_twistGrading 𝒜 hf t)

/-- **The generator is the integer power `f ^ t`**, read in the base-change model. -/
public theorem twistAwayEquiv_twistGen (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (t : ℤ) :
    ((twistAwayEquiv 𝒜 hf t (twistGen 𝒜 hf t) : twistAway 𝒜 f 1 t) : Localization.Away f) =
      ((awayUnit f ^ t : (Localization.Away f)ˣ) : Localization.Away f) := by
  rw [twistAwayEquiv_apply_val, coe_awayUnit_zpow_eq_mk_exp]
  exact localizedAwayEquiv_mk f (f ^ numExp t) _

/-! ### The rank-one basis -/

/-- **The integer power `f ^ t` spans the `t`-th degree part of `A[1/f]`.** At degree one every
integer is a multiple of the degree, so `Stacks.GradedLaurent.twistAway_eq_span_zpow` applies with
no divisibility condition. -/
public theorem span_range_const_eq_twistAway (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (t : ℤ) :
    Submodule.span (Away 𝒜 f) (Set.range fun _ : Unit =>
        ((awayUnit f ^ t : (Localization.Away f)ˣ) : Localization.Away f)) =
      twistAway 𝒜 f 1 t := by
  have h := twistAway_eq_span_zpow 𝒜 hf t
  rw [Nat.cast_one, mul_one] at h
  rw [Set.range_const, h]

/-- The integer power `f ^ t` is linearly independent over the degree-zero localization, as a
one-element family. -/
public theorem linearIndependent_const_awayUnit_zpow (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (t : ℤ) :
    LinearIndependent (Away 𝒜 f) (fun _ : Unit =>
      ((awayUnit f ^ t : (Localization.Away f)ˣ) : Localization.Away f)) := by
  have h := (linearIndependent_coe_awayUnit_zpow 𝒜 hf one_ne_zero).comp
    (fun _ : Unit => t) (fun _ _ _ => Subsingleton.elim _ _)
  simpa [Function.comp_def] using h

/-- **The `t`-th degree part of `A[1/f]` is free of rank one on `f ^ t`**, for `f` homogeneous of
degree one. -/
public def twistAwayBasis (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (t : ℤ) :
    Module.Basis Unit (Away 𝒜 f) (twistAway 𝒜 f 1 t) :=
  (Module.Basis.span (linearIndependent_const_awayUnit_zpow 𝒜 hf t)).map
    (LinearEquiv.ofEq _ _ (span_range_const_eq_twistAway 𝒜 hf t))

/-- The basis vector of the base-change model is the integer power `f ^ t`. -/
public theorem twistAwayBasis_apply (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (t : ℤ) (u : Unit) :
    ((twistAwayBasis 𝒜 hf t u : twistAway 𝒜 f 1 t) : Localization.Away f) =
      ((awayUnit f ^ t : (Localization.Away f)ˣ) : Localization.Away f) := by
  rw [twistAwayBasis, Module.Basis.map_apply, Module.Basis.span_apply]
  rfl

/-- **The chart sections of the `t`-th twist are free of rank one on the generator**, for `f`
homogeneous of degree one: the basis of the base-change model, transported along the
identification of the two models. -/
public def twistDegreeZeroBasis (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (t : ℤ) :
    Module.Basis Unit (Away 𝒜 f)
      (GradedModuleDegreeZeroLocalization 𝒜 (twistGrading (S := A) 𝒜 t) f) :=
  (twistAwayBasis 𝒜 hf t).map (twistAwayEquiv 𝒜 hf t).symm

/-- **The basis vector of the chart-sections model is the generator.** -/
public theorem twistDegreeZeroBasis_apply (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (t : ℤ) (u : Unit) :
    twistDegreeZeroBasis 𝒜 hf t u = twistGen 𝒜 hf t := by
  rw [twistDegreeZeroBasis, Module.Basis.map_apply]
  refine (twistAwayEquiv 𝒜 hf t).symm_apply_eq.mpr (Subtype.ext ?_)
  rw [twistAwayEquiv_twistGen, twistAwayBasis_apply]

/-- **The chart sections of the `t`-th twist are free over the chart ring**, for `f` homogeneous
of degree one. -/
public theorem free_twistDegreeZero (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (t : ℤ) :
    Module.Free (Away 𝒜 f)
      (GradedModuleDegreeZeroLocalization 𝒜 (twistGrading (S := A) 𝒜 t) f) :=
  Module.Free.of_basis (twistDegreeZeroBasis 𝒜 hf t)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartDegreeOne

end
